    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triage new Gmail emails with AI labels and priority using Gemini\n\nEvery new email gets a category label and, when it matters, a high-priority label. VIP senders and urgent keywords always rank high, junk can be archived, urgent mail pings you, and an 8am digest tells you what needs attention.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Gmail Trigger checks every minute for unread inbox emails (not from you).\n2. **Clean email text and flag VIPs** keeps the new part of each message and flags VIP senders and urgent keywords from your settings.\n3. Gemini returns JSON: a category (needs reply, action, FYI, newsletter, receipt, promotion), a priority and a one-line summary.\n4. Gmail labels are matched by name. VIPs and keywords force high priority.\n5. Labels are added; `archive_categories` are removed from the inbox (never deleted).\n6. Every email is logged to a Google Sheet; urgent ones trigger an alert email to you.\n7. At 8am a digest of the last 24 hours is emailed to you.\n\n### Setup\n1. In Gmail, create these labels: `AI/Needs reply`, `AI/Action`, `AI/FYI`, `AI/Newsletter`, `AI/Receipt`, `AI/Promotion` and `AI/High priority`.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a `Log` tab with the header row: logged_at, from, subject, category, priority, summary, archived, why_high, gmail_link. Put its ID in the two Sheets nodes.\n3. Add Gmail OAuth2, Google Sheets and Google Gemini (free key from aistudio.google.com) credentials.\n4. In **Set your labels and context** set your VIP senders (addresses or @domains), urgent keywords, archive categories and `alert_email`. Set the same email in **Set digest settings**.\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n- Leave `archive_categories` empty to never archive.\n- Edit the categories in the prompt and the `NAMES` map together.",
        "height": 1056,
        "width": 580
      },
